{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nThe recovered 2026-08-16 janitor plan contains approved-but-lossy RP-02 through RP-06 decisions. Before these items become implementation stories, the maintainer needs evidence-backed discussions that preserve prior architectural intent, cover hard-won bug and test behavior, and resolve implementation-critical ambiguities. Durable recovery authority is the closed tracker record `irascible-clueless-basenji` (`ee98-a2c0-7d12-4c75`), whose description and comments record the recovered RP definitions and evidence. The checkout-local `.joe-janitor/report-2026-08-16-recovered.md` is an operator-supplied ignored working copy; if it is absent in another checkout, the durable ticket plus the source/ADR/test/ticket citations it names are sufficient to reconstruct it.\n\n## Approach\nResearch each RP independently against current source, focused behavioral tests, ticket/ADR/commit history, and relevant maintained-project prior art. Record a decision-ready brief per RP under the checkout-local `.joe-janitor/` archive, with the situation, intended end state, invariants versus intentional behavior changes, edge/failure scenarios, concrete implementation seams, migration/rollback considerations, and remaining maintainer-only decisions. Use read-only or checkout-local probes where framework behavior is uncertain. This fits the janitor approval phase because it reduces ambiguity without editing production code or prematurely creating implementation stories.\n\n## Scope\nNo tracked repository file changes. Read-only scope includes `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/`, `src/rebar/_cli/`, `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/`, their focused tests, `docs/adr/`, exact historical tickets/commits, and the durable recovery ticket. Outputs live in checkout-local ignored `.joe-janitor/rp02-*.md` through `.joe-janitor/rp06-*.md` when available and in durable comments on this ticket.\n\n## Verification\nThis is an investigation task. Evidence crosses source boundaries through focused existing tests and narrowly scoped checkout-local probes. The oracles are exact current outcomes, failure modes, ownership boundaries, call/reference inventories, and cited historical decisions. Any behavior change is labeled as a maintainer decision rather than silently treated as an invariant. Each local brief is read back and summarized durably on this ticket; the ticket summary is the portable completion record when ignored artifacts are unavailable to an attested reviewer.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] [operator-attested] RP-02 has a decision-ready brief mapping BindingStore responsibilities, atomicity constraints, prior ADR/ticket intent, focused test oracles, extraction seams, migration hazards, and remaining choices; verified by read-back of its local note and durable ticket summary.\n  provenance: environment=local-checkout-b0aac2314; principal=joeoakhart@navapbc.com; privilege_posture=narrower; instrument=static-analysis — read back the ignored local note and compare its citations and decisions to repository evidence and the live tracker.\n- [ ] [operator-attested] RP-03 has a decision-ready brief mapping outbound lifecycle protocol calls, lossy failure paths, resurrection/idempotency scenarios, prior ticket intent, focused test oracles, migration hazards, and remaining choices; verified by read-back of its local note and durable ticket summary.\n  provenance: environment=local-checkout-b0aac2314; principal=joeoakhart@navapbc.com; privilege_posture=narrower; instrument=static-analysis — read back the ignored local note and compare its citations and decisions to repository evidence and the live tracker.\n- [ ] [operator-attested] RP-04 has a decision-ready brief mapping configured versus ambient tracker/Jira ownership, all bypass call sites, mixed-context failure scenarios, prior ADR/ticket intent, focused test oracles, migration hazards, and remaining choices; verified by read-back of its local note and durable ticket summary.\n  provenance: environment=local-checkout-b0aac2314; principal=joeoakhart@navapbc.com; privilege_posture=narrower; instrument=static-analysis — read back the ignored local note and compare its citations and decisions to repository evidence and the live tracker.\n- [ ] [operator-attested] RP-05 has a decision-ready brief mapping CLI routing responsibilities and compatibility seams, prior split history, focused test oracles, extraction alternatives, migration hazards, and remaining choices; verified by read-back of its local note and durable ticket summary.\n  provenance: environment=local-checkout-b0aac2314; principal=joeoakhart@navapbc.com; privilege_posture=narrower; instrument=static-analysis — read back the ignored local note and compare its citations and decisions to repository evidence and the live tracker.\n- [ ] [operator-attested] RP-06 has a decision-ready brief mapping plan-review policy ownership, registry/orchestrator/facade coupling, routing divergence, compatibility constraints, focused test oracles, extraction alternatives, migration hazards, and remaining choices; verified by read-back of its local note and durable ticket summary.\n  provenance: environment=local-checkout-b0aac2314; principal=joeoakhart@navapbc.com; privilege_posture=narrower; instrument=static-analysis — read back the ignored local note and compare its citations and decisions to repository evidence and the live tracker.\n- [ ] [operator-attested] Every substantive claim cites repository, tracker, history, test, or maintained-project evidence, and every behavior delta is explicitly marked for maintainer approval; verified by a citation/decision-queue audit recorded on this ticket.\n  provenance: environment=local-checkout-b0aac2314; principal=joeoakhart@navapbc.com; privilege_posture=narrower; instrument=static-analysis — compare all durable ticket summaries against their local briefs and cited evidence.\n- [ ] [operator-attested] The durable completion comment links the local RP-02-RP-06 brief paths, states their approval-readiness status, and identifies the recovery ticket that defines their scope; verified by live ticket read-back.\n  provenance: environment=local-checkout-b0aac2314; principal=joeoakhart@navapbc.com; privilege_posture=narrower; instrument=live-call — read the posted comment from the live tracker and compare it to the five local briefs and `irascible-clueless-basenji`."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786911806344997001,"uuid":"0b11ed60-3ed6-4a91-b6ea-107888fc51f7"}